-- title:
--   Hecke legs span the roof field by d elements
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which is assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise extension of $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ the ratios of integral forms for $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \ne p$, and write $K_\ell$ for the analogous base change to $L$ of the field of $q$-expansions attached to $\Gamma_1(Mp) \cap \Gamma_0(Mp\ell)$. Let $\iota : K \to K_\ell$ be an $L$-algebra homomorphism which, on underlying Laurent series, is either the identity, $\iota(f) = f$ for all $f \in K$, or the substitution $q \mapsto q^\ell$, that is $\iota(f) =$ [`ModularCurve.qExpand L ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25) applied to $f$, the ring homomorphism of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ multiplying exponents by $\ell$. Put $d = \ell$ if $\ell \mid M$ and $d = \ell + 1$ otherwise. Then there exists a family $b : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to K_\ell$ such that every $z \in K_\ell$ can be written as $z = \sum_i \iota(c_i)\, b_i$ for some $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to K$. Only spanning is asserted, not linear independence of the $b_i$.
--
--   The statement records that along either degeneracy (Hecke) leg from the modular function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ to that of $\Gamma_1(Mp) \cap \Gamma_0(Mp\ell)$, the upper field is generated as a module over the image of the lower one by $d = [\Gamma_1(Mp) : \Gamma_1(Mp) \cap \Gamma_0(Mp\ell)]$ elements, the index being $\ell$ or $\ell+1$ according as $\ell$ divides $M$ or not. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_span_and_residueIndependent_gauss_heckeRoof_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_span_and_residueIndependent_gauss_heckeRoof_x1_mul).
